<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sand River Convention</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1852">1852</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sand River Convention was an agreement signed on 17 January 1852 between British commissioners and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> leaders headed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andries-pretorius">Andries Pretorius</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> recognised the independence of the emigrant Boers living north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vaal-river">Vaal River</a>, undertook not to ally with African peoples beyond it, and agreed that the Boers could buy ammunition while Africans could not. It led to the founding of the South African Republic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sand-river-convention.jpg" alt="Sand River Convention" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: JMK · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sandrivierkonvensie,_paneel_27,_Voortrekkermonument,_a.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
